    "result": "Perfect! The bug has been fixed successfully.\n\n## Summary\n\n**The Problem:** The `frai gate init --ci` command wasn't creating the GitHub Actions workflow file (`.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`). The `--ci` flag wasn't being passed through from the `frai` CLI to the underlying `frai-gate` CLI.\n\n**The Root Cause:** In the original code, the action handler for the `gate` command only passed the positional `args` array to the spawned `frai-gate` process. The `--ci` flag wasn't being included because Commander.js consumed it during parsing but didn't make it available through the normal parameters.\n\n**The Fix:** Modified `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (lines 752-753) to directly extract all arguments after 'gate' from `process.argv`, ensuring all original command-line arguments (including unknown flags like `--ci`) are passed through unchanged to the `frai-gate` CLI.\n\n**Verification:** The fix has been rebuilt and tested:\n- \u2705 Running `frai gate init --ci` now creates `FRAI-SPEC.md`\n- \u2705 Running `frai gate init --ci` now creates `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`\n- \u2705 The workflow file contains the correct GitHub Actions configuration",
